 {"id": "PEDS-U433", "ch": 53, "n": 4, "title": "Airway, Breathing & ET Intubation", "sec": "Airway, breathing and intubation · p254", "guide": "Airway: head tilt–chin lift first, then jaw thrust. Breathing is non-invasive (bag-and-mask ventilation) or invasive (endotracheal intubation, preferred in hospital CPR and prolonged CPR). The tube is cuffed with size (Age + 4)/4, cuff pressure below 20–25 cm H2O to prevent pressure necrosis, and depth of insertion 3 × Age in years. Routine cricoid pressure is avoided (cartilage damage); breathing rate is 20–30/min, i.e. one breath every 2–3 seconds.", "qs": ["PEDS-C53-065", "PEDS-C53-066", "PEDS-C53-067", "PEDS-C53-068", "PEDS-C53-069", "PEDS-C53-070", "PEDS-C53-071", "PEDS-C53-072", "PEDS-C53-073", "PEDS-C53-074", "PEDS-C53-075", "PEDS-C53-076", "PEDS-C53-077", "PEDS-C53-078", "PEDS-C53-079", "PEDS-C53-080", "PEDS-C53-081", "PEDS-C53-082", "PEDS-C53-083", "PEDS-C53-084", "PEDS-C53-085", "PEDS-C53-086"]},
