 {"sec": "Airway, breathing and intubation · p254", "page": 254, "q": "Match each intubation parameter with its value:", "opts": ["A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1", "A-1, B-4, C-3, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2", "A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Tube type, size, cuff and depth are all specified. Correct pairs: Tube type→Cuffed; Tube size→Age plus 4 divided by 4; Cuff pressure→Below 20–25 cm of H2O; Depth of insertion→3 times Age in years. (Book p254)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Tube type", "Below 20–25 cm of H2O"], ["Tube size", "3 times Age in years"], ["Cuff pressure", "Cuffed"], ["Depth of insertion", "Age plus 4 divided by 4"]], "id": "PEDS-C53-082"},
 {"sec": "Airway, breathing and intubation · p254", "page": 254, "q": "True or False — Uncuffed tubes are preferred per the chapter.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — type of tube: cuffed. (Book p254)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C53-083"},
 {"sec": "Airway, breathing and intubation · p254", "page": 254, "q": "Per the chapter, the tube size is calculated by:", "opts": ["(Age + 4)/4", "20–30", "Under 10 sec", "3 × Age"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Size = (Age + 4)/4; 3 × Age is the depth of insertion. (Book p254)", "type": "case", "stem": "An 8-year-old in prolonged in-hospital CPR needs endotracheal intubation.", "id": "PEDS-C53-084"},
