 {"sec": "Vascular access, AED and rhythms · p255", "page": 255, "q": "Match each rhythm with its class and pattern:", "opts": ["A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1", "A-1, B-4, C-3, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Wide-QRS rhythms shock; flat or organised pulseless rhythms do not. Correct pairs: Ventricular fibrillation→Shockable with irregular rhythm; Pulseless VT→Shockable with regular rhythm; Asystole→Non-shockable flat rhythm; PEA→Non-shockable organised rhythm. (Book p255)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Ventricular fibrillation", "Non-shockable flat rhythm"], ["Pulseless VT", "Non-shockable organised rhythm"], ["Asystole", "Shockable with irregular rhythm"], ["PEA", "Shockable with regular rhythm"]], "id": "PEDS-C53-103"},
